  "notes": "Viewed all 192 actual native material-readback PNGs at 160x160 nearest-neighbor display in three 64-case sheets. Admitted as a reference-program/control-learning bootstrap: distinct primary motif families, central/offset/split/border layouts, repeatable symmetry and central voids are visible. Native success is independently verified. This is labeled assistant inspection, not blind recognition, human artistic approval or per-modifier visual review. Exact duplicate native readbacks are reported separately and are not used as artistic quality proof.",
  "quality_limits": [
    "Coral defaults form a crowded lower band with a large upper void; sparse coral is more legible.",
    "Narrow border strips compress facets, dunes and ribs; their primary morphology can become weak or barcode-like.",
